<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21868" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενέσι-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενέθλιος, θεός</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				402a
			</span></i>; epith. of Posidon, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				2.38.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γενέσιον, τό</span>, shrine of Posidon <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γ.</span>, Paus.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενέσια, τά</span>, <i>day kept in memory of the birthday of the
				dead</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.26
			</span></i>, cf. Ammon.<i><span class="en">
				p.36V.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				83
			</span></i>; to be distinguished from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενέθλια</span>
			<i>birthday-feast</i>, though used for it in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				784d
			</span></i> (s. v. l.) and later Gk., <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				736.56
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">i B. C.</span><span class="entity">/i A. D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PFay.</u>
				114.20
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i/ii A. D.)</span>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.18
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				14.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				6.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				47.18
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γ. ἡμέρα,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γενέθλιος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2883c
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Branchidae</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ γ.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				583.14
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyprus</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ τοῦ Σεβαστοῦ ἐμμήνῳ γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IGRom.</u>
					4.353b
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam., <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
